0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","article",null,{"className":"pt-32","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"container-site max-w-3xl","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mono-label text-ink-muted","children":["June 22, 2026"," · ",1," ","min read"]}],["$","$L2",null,{"as":"h1","variant":"clip","className":"mt-6 font-serif text-display text-ink","children":"What changed when I went from enterprise Angular to freelance React"}],["$","$L2",null,{"as":"p","delay":0.15,"className":"mt-6 text-body-lg text-ink-muted","children":"Five and a half years inside a large delivery organisation taught me one set of habits. Working directly with founders taught me which of them were load-bearing."}]]}],null,["$","div",null,{"className":"container-site section-pad","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"prose-content space-y-6 text-ink [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:text-ink [&_h2]:mt-12 [&_h3]:font-semibold [&_img]:rounded-xl [&_a]:text-accent-strong [&_a]:underline-offset-4 hover:[&_a]:underline mx-auto max-w-3xl","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"payload-richtext","children":[["$","p","0",{"children":["In an enterprise delivery team, the work arrives shaped. Someone has already decided what is being built and why; your job is to build it well, at scale, without breaking the things around it. That is a real skill, and it is not the same skill as deciding what to build."]}],["$","p","1",{"children":["Since February 2025 I have worked directly with founders and small businesses. The brief now arrives as a problem, not a ticket. A restaurant group does not ask for a booking flow — they ask why the phone rings all evening. Half the value is in translating that into something buildable, and the translation is my job now too."]}],["$","p","2",{"children":["The technical habits that survived the switch were the boring ones: type everything, keep the boundaries explicit, write the test that would have caught it. The habits that did not survive were the ceremonial ones — the estimates nobody used, the documents written for an audience that never read them."]}],["$","p","3",{"children":["The thing I underestimated was scope. On a small project there is no product manager standing between an idea and the codebase, so scope moves every week unless you hold it. Saying no to a feature is now part of the work, not an escalation."]}],["$","p","4",{"children":["What I kept from the enterprise years is a tolerance for systems that have to keep running. Enterprise code is not glamorous, but it teaches you that shipping is not the end of the job — the thing has to survive Monday morning without you."]}]]}]}]}]]}],[["$","script","script-0",{"src":"/_next/static/chunks/138yfan2wekri.js","async":true}]],["$","$L3",null,{"children":["$","$4",null,{"name":"Next.MetadataOutlet","children":"$@5"}]}]]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"S3ldyZsaGSR339Cj2StMi"}
